@format 1
@id media-loading.in-merge-tab
@title In Merge tab
@section Media loading
@area In Merge tab
@entry merge-path-change, merge-group-row, merge-group-drop, merge-items-add
@summary Show Merge-specific selected-path/group loading, external group drops, and the PListItemsAdd auto-group update.
@related media-loading.common.files-intake, media-loading.common.docket-insertion, media-loading.common.files-selection, media-loading.common.viewer-gate, media-loading.common.file-drops
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag merge

@alias merge = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PMergeTab
@alias group = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PGroup
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList

[merge-path-change] Merge Files current-path event <input>
= PListPathChange delivered the current path to PMergePathShow.
> merge-path-result

[merge-group-row] Merge grouped-item selection <input>
- Emit the selected grouped media path and forward it through PMergePathShow @ group.PGroupFileBuild(...)
  @ merge.PMergePathShow(...)
> map:media-loading.common.viewer-gate

[merge-group-drop] External file drop on Merge group <input>
- Receive a file-system drop on the group area or an existing group card; PGroupPathsRead invokes the Merge PGroupFileRequest delegate @ group.PGroupDropHandle(...)
  @ group.PGroupCardHandle(...)
  @ group.PGroupPathsRead(...)
> merge-group-files

[merge-items-add] Merge newly-added-items event <input>
= PListItemsAdd reached PMergeItemsHandle after first-new-item PListPathChange returned.
> merge-auto-result

[merge-path-result] Merge selected-path adapter <decision>
- Ignore blank paths; otherwise request the Merge viewer source @ merge.PMergePathShow(...)
? "Nonblank current path" > map:media-loading.common.viewer-gate
? "Blank current path" > merge-no-request

[merge-group-files] Merge group file-request delegate <process>
- The delegate first calls PListPathsAdd, whose complete Files intake and Docket insertion notifications run synchronously before it returns; it then calls PListMediaScan a second time and returns those scanned paths to PGroupPathsRead for group insertion @ list.PListPathsAdd(...)
  @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
! Common / Files intake details the first call. The second scan supplies the paths that PGroupCardHandle or PGroupDropHandle inserts into group state.
> merge-group-inserted

[merge-auto-result] Auto grouping enabled <decision>
- PMergeItemsHandle updates group auto-classification only when the Merge group owner currently has auto grouping enabled @ merge.PMergeItemsHandle(...)
? "Auto grouping enabled" > merge-auto-update
? "Auto grouping disabled" > merge-auto-nochange

[merge-no-request] Merge viewer request omitted <output>
= Merge does not call the shared viewer-loading pipeline.

[merge-group-inserted] External paths returned to group handler <output>
= The group handler inserts the second-scan paths into the target/new group and rebuilds the group UI; any media loading caused by Files insertion occurred earlier during PListPathsAdd.

[merge-auto-update] Recompute automatic groups <process>
- Rebuild automatic grouping after the new docket entries were announced @ group.PGroupAutoUpdate(...)
> merge-auto-complete

[merge-auto-nochange] Auto grouping unchanged <output>
= PListItemsAdd causes no grouping update while auto grouping is disabled.

[merge-auto-complete] Automatic groups updated <output>
= Merge grouping reflects the newly added Files entries.
